      <h2>2. Indicative freight rates from China to Germany</h2>
      <p>
        Unlike some smaller corridors, Germany has published benchmark depth: the WorldFreightHub Europe
        route data carries Hamburg ranges of <strong>$1,200–$4,600 for a 20ft</strong>,
        <strong>$1,600–$6,500 for a 40ft</strong> and <strong>$60–$150 per CBM for LCL</strong>, all
        MEDIUM confidence. Rail is described in relative terms — roughly two to three times sea per
        container — but has no published dollar figure, and air, express and DDP were not published in the
        snapshot, so those stay LOW with a request-for-quote marker.
      </p>

