    <h2>3. Transit times by origin port and mode</h2>
    <p>
      The China-to-Germany clock is a planning range, not a promise, and 2026 made the Cape routing a new
      normal rather than a blip. The WorldFreightHub Europe route data puts sea transit at roughly
      <strong>30–38 days via the Cape of Good Hope</strong>, with the Red Sea reroute adding about
      <strong>+10–14 days</strong> versus the pre-crisis Suez routing. Rail from Xi\u2019an or Chengdu to
      Hamburg runs roughly <strong>18–22 days</strong>. German air transit is not published, so that line
      stays explicit instead of borrowing a neighbouring airport figure.
    </p>

